update investigationfinding set findingcomments = 'CHILD NEGLECT-UNSUBSTANTIATED

	Child neglect of _Tyler Roscoe (DOB: 11/4/10) and Tristen (DOB: 6/26/12_ is ruled unsubstantiated, in accordance with the provisions of Family Law Article 5-701 (U) and COMAR 07.02.07.16 (B).
(1)	It is the professional assessment of this worker that there is insufficient evidence to support a finding of indicated in that:

a.	It is not possible to complete the investigation due to an inability to gain access to the child or to obtain relevant facts regarding the reported incident or circumstances alleged to be neglectful. It was reported that Ms. Jones left her five children ages twelve to five years old unattended at home. This worker made multiple attempts to visit with Ms. Jones and her children under an Alternative Response. When Ms. Jones did not respond to this worker the case was changed to an investigation. Ms. Jones told Afterhours CPS Worker S. Wise that her sister (name unknown) was supposed to be watching her children as she was deployed to work. However, this worker has no evidence of this as Ms. Jones never met with this worker to complete an assessment. As such, the case is unsubstantiated. 
AND
(2)	There is insufficient evidence to support a finding of ruled out, in that Sgt Franks reported finding the children home alone at 8:30pm on 5/17/17. Ms. Jones was contacted at her place of employment and she responded to her home where the children were alone.



Identification of an Alleged Neglector:
	As a result of this investigation Ciara Jones is identified as an alleged neglector, in that it is more likely than not that Ms. Jones failed to provide proper care and attention, but there is insufficient evidence to determine by a preponderance of the evidence that the improper care and attention was caused under circumstances which indicate that the childs health or welfare was harmed or placed at substantial risk of harm.
', updatedon = now(), updatedby = 'CDM-4638' where investigationfindingid = 'e17b2da7-967a-4cec-9a18-dcca39e8317a';


